1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[narrator] Ten:

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
The ability to envelop your body
in a shroud of Nen aura,

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
making it tougher and slowing
the effects of aging.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Zetsu:

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
A technique which shuts off
your flow of Nen aura.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Effective for concealing your presence
and recovering from fatigue.

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Ren:

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
A technique for creating
an especially strong Nen aura.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
It is crucial for increasing your power.

10
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Hatsu:

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The release of your Nen aura
after using Ren to boost it.

12
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
These four elements
are known as the Four Exercises

13
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
and are critical to the mastery of Nen.

14
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
[theme song playing]

15
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
[clapping]

16
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Splendid. Just splendid.

17
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Including your last two matches,

18
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
you’ve made progress.

19
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
You’ve made the grade,
so set the place of your choosing.

20
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
I’ll take you on any time.

21
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
[determined grunt]

22
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
THE x TRUE x PASS

23
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
[narrator] Hisoka finally consents
to a fight with Gon,

24
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:44,000
who prepares by continuing
to train tirelessly in the use of Nen.

25
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
[Wing] Today we’re going
to begin our study of Hatsu.

26
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Once you master Hatsu,

27
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
then you will have mastered
all of the basics of Nen.

28
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
At that point in your education

29
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
you’ll need to start developing
your own Nen style.

30
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,000
[Gon, Zushi and Killua] Osu!

31
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,000
[Wing] Hatsu is the technique
by which you control your aura.

32
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
In other words,
it’s the culmination of Nen abilities

33
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
of which there are six categories.

34
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Enhancers strengthen and reinforce
natural abilities.

35
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Emitters propel aura.

36
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Transmuters change the quality of aura.

37
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Conjurers materialize objects out of aura.

38
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Manipulators control things with aura.

39
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,000
And Specialists are those
with a unique and distinct aura

40
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
that doesn’t fall
within the other five classes.

41
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
It’s incredibly important
that you find an ability that suits you.

42
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
What do you mean, ‘suits you’?

43
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
[Wing] Nen abilities are highly personal

44
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
with two areas of particular prominence.

45
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
The ability that you’re born with

46
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,000
and of course, the ability
you’ve refined later in life.

47
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,000
For example:

48
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Gon here was born with muscles

49
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
that are more flexible and springy
than most.

50
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:08,000
His acute senses were honed
by a childhood spent mostly in nature.

51
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
So, you see, from the moment of birth

52
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
your Nen ability falls
within one of the six categories.

53
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
It’s possible for your Nen aura
to change types later on,

54
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
although that’s quite rare.

55
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
If you attempt to learn a new ability,

56
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
one that doesn’t fit your natural aura,

57
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
you will have a hard time.

58
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
This depicts the compatibility
of the six categories.

59
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
The closer a class is to your own,

60
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
the greater your chances of learning it.

61
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,000
If you are born with an aura
of the Enhancer category,

62
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:48,000
you will find Enhancer abilities
easiest to learn and master.

63
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
The adjacent Transmuter
and Emitter classes

64
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
will also be easy to pick up.

65
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,000
On the other hand,

66
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
the Specialist class,
which is furthest away,

67
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
would undoubtedly prove quite difficult.

68
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
I’ll demonstrate using skills
you’ve already seen.

69
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Hisoka is able to change his aura
into a rubber-like substance.

70
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,000
So, he’s a Transmuter.

71
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Gido uses his tops as a weapon
by making them spin faster,

72
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
which is an Enhancer power.

73
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,000
But trying to manipulate so many tops
as weapons

74
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
also requires the skill of a Manipulator.

75
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Since that isn’t very compatible,
he wasn’t very effective.

76
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,000
As for Kastro,

77
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,000
his Tiger Bite Fist was incredibly strong.

78
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Had he mastered it,

79
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
he would have been
among the strongest Nen users.

80
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
I believe that his aura
fell into the Enhancer class.

81
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
However, he made the choice

82
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
to focus his energy on the power
to create a double,

83
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
which is a Conjurer ability.

84
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,000
He also required
the ability of a Manipulator

85
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
to control the double.

86
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,000
As you can see,

87
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,000
both of those are relatively far
from the Enhancer category.

88
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
[Gon] So neither of them
was compatible with an Enhancer type?

89
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Correct.

90
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Learning an incompatible ability

91
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:09,000
requires a great deal
of work and natural talent.

92
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
As a result of the focus of his training,

93
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
he squandered most of his talent
in Nen ability.

94
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,000
What you’re saying is,

95
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Kastro made the wrong choice.

96
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
He was such a great fighter.

97
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,000
What a shame.

98
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
What do you think?

99
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Are you all
beginning to see the importance

100
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,000
of fully understanding your own aura
as well as its nature?

101
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
[Gon and Zushi] Osu!

102
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
[Killua] Okay, so…

103
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:35,000
if you don’t know your aura’s type,
like, what category it’s in,

104
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,000
is there a way to find out?

105
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,000
There is.

106
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Water Divination,

107
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
a Shingen-ryu screening tool
for classifying aura.

108
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
It’s also used in training Hatsu.

109
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Perform Ren with your hands
placed on either side of the glass.

110
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:59,000
Your ability will be revealed
by what happens.

111
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,000
[Gon] The water’s overflowing!

112
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
[Wing] If the volume of water changes,

113
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
then you’re an Enhancer.

114
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:21,000
This change demonstrates that my aura
falls within the Enhancer category.

115
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Okay. Now it’s time for you to try.

116
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
So Gon’s an Enhancer, too?

117
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
-[Killua] Hm?
-[Zushi] The leaf moved!

118
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:49,000
That movement indicates
that you’re a Manipulator.

119
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
All right, then. That just leaves me.

120
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
[focusing grunt]

121
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
What gives? Nothing’s happening.

122
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,000
[Wing] Indeed…

123
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
The leaf isn’t moving either…

124
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Does that mean…
I don’t have what it takes?

125
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,000
Oh, no.

126
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Try tasting the water, Killua.

127
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
[Killua] Taste it?

128
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
Hey… I think it might’ve gotten sweeter.

129
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Yeah, you’re right!

130
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
That’s true. It does taste sweet.

131
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Wait… then this isn’t plain water?

132
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Perfectly ordinary.

133
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Only the taste of it has changed…

134
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
due to Killua’s aura.

135
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,000
What does that mean?

136
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
[Wing] It means you’re a Transmuter.

137
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Wow!

138
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
You’re a Transmuter?

139
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Okay. Now the three of you know exactly
what kind of aura you’re working with.

140
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,000
For the next four weeks,

141
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
I want you three to train

142
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,000
until you can make
a more pronounced change in the water.

143
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,000
[Gon, Zushi and Killua] Osu!

144
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
JUNE 11

145
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
JUNE 16

146
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
JUNE 20

147
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
[phone ringing]

148
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,000
[Gon] Hello? This is Gon.

149
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
[Hisoka] Hey… I’ve been waiting.

150
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
So? Have you made a decision?

151
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
[Gon] Yeah. July 10th.

152
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,000
That’s the day I’ve chosen!

153
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,000
[chuckles]

154
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,000
Okay.

155
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
I’ll be looking forward to it.

156
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
JUNE 22

157
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:11,000
[focusing grunt]

158
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[tired exhale]

159
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
[solemn grunt]

160
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
JUNE 30

161
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[focusing grunt]

162
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
JULY 5

163
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Okay. Time to see what you’ve accomplished
with your training.

164
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,000
-Killua, you're up first.
-All right.

165
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,000
I'm done.

166
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,000
So sweet!

167
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
You’re right! It tastes like honey!

168
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Excellent. And Zushi?

169
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,000
[Zushi] Osu!

170
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:08,000
[straining grunt]

171
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
[Gon] Whoa!

172
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
[straining grunt]

173
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
[exhausted exhale, defeated sigh]

174
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
That’s the best I can do!

175
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
That’s all right.

176
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
But it isn’t going to be enough to pass.

177
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
I’m afraid you’ll need to train
a bit more.

178
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Osu.

179
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Next… Gon.

180
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Osu!

181
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
[glass crackles]

182
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
[both gasp]

183
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Stop! Gon, stop!

184
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:59,000
The water increased so forcefully
it cracked the glass.

185
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Honestly...

186
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,000
I’m impressed!

187
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
I was feeling pretty good about this.

188
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,000
All right, Gon, Killua.

189
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Today, you are both graduating.

190
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
-Oh...
-Really?

191
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
-We did it, Killua!
-That’s awesome!!

192
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Master… Do I graduate, too?

193
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:22,000
You still need to train
a little bit longer.

194
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Osu…

195
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Just keep at it.

196
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Yeah. You’ll get it!

197
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Osu...

198
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
-And Gon…
-Oh?

199
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,000
I’ve one more thing for you.

200
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Something important I still need to say.

201
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,000
What is it, Mr. Wing?

202
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,000
The Other Hunter Exam…

203
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
You’ve passed it...

204
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Gon Freecss.

205
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Congratulations.

206
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,000
You made it!

207
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,000
[Gon] The Other Hunter Exam?

208
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
That’s correct.

209
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
You were able to pass with flying colors.

210
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,000
What do you mean, sir?

211
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:03,000
One cannot be a full-fledged Hunter
without learning how to use Nen.

212
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:07,000
Such skill and power are requirements
of a terribly dangerous profession.

213
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,000
One of your duties as a Hunter

214
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:14,000
will be attempting to apprehend
evil poachers and other such criminals.

215
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:18,000
You must be strong enough to fight crime
if you are to be a true deterrent.

216
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,000
But this power is highly destructive
when abused.

217
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Revealing the existence of Nen
during the Exam

218
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
would be quite risky.

219
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Therefore, only those
who have already passed the Main Exam

220
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
are tested.

221
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,000
Oh, I get it.

222
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
You would’ve tested us,
Gon at least,

223
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,000
no matter what happened, wouldn’t you?

224
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,000
[Wing] Yes.

225
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:42,000
I should also have mentioned
that the Grand Master of Shingen-ryu

226
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
happens to be Chairman Netero.

227
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,000
[Gon and Killua gasp]

228
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:47,000
[Wing]
The master has told me so much about you.

229
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
That goofy old man?

230
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
[Wing] Killua.

231
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,000
[Killua] What?

232
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,000
I want you to go back
and take the Hunter Exam again.

233
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
You’ll definitely pass next time.

234
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
-Oh...
-He’s right!

235
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
At this point,
you are more than qualified enough.

236
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
That I can guarantee.

237
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Well… if I feel up to it.

238
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,000
[Gon] Hey, Mr. Wing?

239
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Have you heard anything
about any of the other people who passed?

240
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
I have.

241
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Hanzo and Kurapika

242
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
have learned Nen from other teachers.

243
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,000
Pokkle, on the other hand,
is struggling with Ren.

244
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,000
Leorio has begun studying
for the medical school exam.

245
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Hisoka and Illumi were already
well-versed in the use of Nen,

246
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,000
so they were qualified, of course.

247
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,000
[Gon]
So Kurapika and Leorio are working hard!

248
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,000
[Killua] Yeah.

249
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,000
That’s not all, Gon.

250
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
I have one bit of advice.

251
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
When you fight Hisoka tomorrow,

252
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,000
don't push yourself too hard.

253
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,000
-All right?
-Right!

254
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,000
Zushi.

255
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:03,000
You will continue your training
for four more weeks.

256
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,000
Osu...

257
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Have more confidence.

258
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
You’re really progressing
at an incredible pace.

259
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
You’re one in a hundred thousand.

260
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Wait, I’m one in a hundred thousand?!

261
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,000
O-- Osu!

262
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Those two, however…

263
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,000
are even rarer talents.

264
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Perhaps one in ten million.

265
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Osu!

266
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Is that supposed
to make me feel better, Master?

267
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,000
[Zushi] But… One day…

268
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
I’m gonna catch up to both of them!

269
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,000
[Cocco] Hello, everyone!

270
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,000
In the arena today we have a match
between Gon and Hisoka!

271
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
The battle you’ve all been waiting for
is about to begin.

272
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,000
And as you can see, the stands are packed!

273
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:18,000
The fight hasn’t even started
and the tension in the air is palpable!

274
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,000
[spectator 1] How much longer?

275
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,000
[spectator 2] Come on, let’s go!

276
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,000
[flexes knuckles]

277
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:33,000
[determined grunt]

278
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
[cheering]

279
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
[Cocco] The first to arrive is Gon!

280
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
After four fights,
he has a three-one record.

281
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
He’s really on a roll!

282
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,000
[spectator 3] You can do it, Gon!

283
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[spectator 4]
Hey, where’s your fishing rod?

284
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
You can’t catch Hisoka
with your bare hands!

285
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:06,000
[Cocco] And next, arriving in the arena
with a fiery display…

286
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
is Hisoka!

287
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:12,000
[cheering]

288
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,000
[Cocco] The memories
of his lethal battle with Kastro

289
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,000
are still fresh in everyone’s minds!

290
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,000
A nine-three record means a win today

291
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,000
earns him the right
to challenge a Floor Master!

292
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,000
He’s won every single match
he’s actually showed up for.

293
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Will his undefeated streak continue?

294
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:35,000
[cheering]

295
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,000
[Hisoka] Oh...

296
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Don’t look at me like that…

297
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,000
SCHWING

298
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
It’s really turning me on!

299
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
[Wing] What a sinister aura he has.

300
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:03,000
Gon… don’t overdo it.

301
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,000
[audience] Oh!

302
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,000
You win by points or knock out.

303
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,000
No time limit!

304
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,000
One round!

305
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
Begin!

306
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:26,000
[Cocco] This is the match
you’ve been waiting for, folks!

307
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,000
The die has been cast!

308
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Who will make the first move?

309
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,000
It's Gon!

310
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
[Gon grunts]

311
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
[Gon grunting]

312
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:43,000
[short cry of pain]

313
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,000
[grunting]

314
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
[grunt of pain]

315
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,000
[excited roar]

316
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
[Gon grunting]

317
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,000
[roaring]

318
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
[roaring]

319
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,000
[grunt of pain]

320
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,000
[straining]

321
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:40,000
A clean hit! Hisoka: One point!

322
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
[audience roaring]

323
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:45,000
That... was an amazing exchange!

324
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
So amazing that I could barely
get a word in edgewise!

325
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
[chuckling]

326
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,000
What’s the matter?

327
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
I haven’t moved a single step
from where I started.

328
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,000
What? Really?

329
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,000
[grunts]

330
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,000
Dammit!

331
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Well, just you wait!

332
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
[Gon] Okay.

333
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
I shouldn’t have to connect each hit.

334
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,000
I can mix in some feints
to get the same effect.

335
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
[Killua]
Hisoka looks like he’s having fun.

336
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
In terms of actual skill,

337
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:21,000
there’s a world of difference
in their combat experience.

338
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
But he still has a weakness.

339
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Hisoka thinks he’s stronger,

340
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:27,000
so there’s no way he’ll ever back down.

341
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,000
That’ll give Gon a chance...

342
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
[Gon] Fine. I know just the trick!

343
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,000
[roaring]

344
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
[growling]

345
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,000
[Cocco] There it is! Gon’s Stone Flip!

346
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,000
[roaring]

347
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:57,000
[Hisoka] He shattered the tile
to create a hail of rubble.

348
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Gon...

349
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Where is he?

350
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:24,000
[no sound]

351
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:38,000
[narrator] Gon has finally landed
a critical hit on Hisoka.

352
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
But the match has only just begun...

353
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:43,000
and it won’t be long

354
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:46,000
before Gon experiences
Hisoka’s true power.

355
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:50,000
[theme song playing]

356
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
[Gon] Coming up:

357
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:59,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

358
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

359
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

360
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

361
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,000
Today, we're introducing Hisoka.

362
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
He reels in opponents
with Rubbery Nen called Bungee Gum.

363
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:11,000
And he uses Texture Surprise
to duplicate other objects.

364
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:13,000
[both] Schween!

365
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,000
[Gon] Next time:
“A Big Debt x And x A Small Kick”!

366
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Killua] Go, Gon, go!

367
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon] Gon Shot!
